<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">necromancer</ansi>

The Necromancer is the elite class of the Warlock (evil wizard route). It
needs alignment -30 or lower at level 30. It drains the living and raises the
dead: a foe that falls in the battle can rise as a thrall (see
<ansi fg="command">help thrall</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Raise the Fallen  once a battle, when a foe has fallen, a 2-round chant
                       (a tenth of its mana) raises it as a thrall with 60% of
                       its health, its weapon attacks and no spells. Bosses
                       can't be raised
  35 Deeper drain      Life Drain heals 150% of the damage it deals, and
                       spells deal 35% more damage in all
  40 Grave Chill       Life Drain also hobbles its first target
  45 Grim rising       a thrall rises with 85% of its health
  50 Raise again       Raise the Fallen twice a battle
  55 Death's Harvest   each foe that falls restores 3% of its mana
  60 Lich's Bargain    once a battle, a blow that would fell the Necromancer
                       leaves it at 1 health, and its thrall (if any) crumbles
                       instead

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

A Necromancer raises a fallen foe before it does anything else, and drains
foes with Life Drain (a Warlock's spell, learned at level 10) while an ally is
hurt. Both are automatic. The raise costs a tenth of its maximum mana and a
blow can break the chant; the fallen foe is remembered until the battle ends.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Wizard elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves, Focused Will, Spell
Edge. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help thrall</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wizard-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
